WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:38,180
The

00:00:52.170 --> 00:01:01.750
year was 1985, and the number one show on
TV was Evil Brat!

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:06.350
The show starred young Balthazar Brat as a
child prodigy.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:22.323
Brat was the biggest
child actor of the 1980s,

00:01:22.324 --> 00:01:25.870
striking a chord with
audiences all over the world.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:35.760
But it all came to an end in Season
3, when... I've been a bad boy!

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.640
The young star experienced an unexpected
growth spurt.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:40.820
The show was cancelled.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.860
Hollywood rejected him, and Brat quickly
plunged into a downward spiral,

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:50.920
starting to actually believe he was the
character he played on TV.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.440
What are you looking at?

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.600
Leading us all to wonder...

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:56.460
Where is he now?

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.980
You know what, Clive?

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:10.760
Playing a villain on TV was fun,
but being one in real life is even better!

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.440
Heist music!

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:13.660
Here he comes!

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.040
Ow!

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:17.560
What?

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.880
Clive, what are you music?

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.560
Sorry, my bad.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.390
I'm scared of you.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:56.780
I'm going to get you!

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:11.950
Sir, the ship has been boarded by some
kind of monster!

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:13.470
Wait, that's not a monster!

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.630
That's a man wearing shoulder pads!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.770
There's only one supervillain whose
fashion sense is quite that dated.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.650
Balthazar Brat!

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.470
Blast it, the Jumont Diamond is on that
ship!

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:29.290
I want every agent in the area on the
scene immediately!

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:35.660
We're here!

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.720
Agents Grucy are closing fast!

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:38.300
Yes!

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:39.620
Wait, why?

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:40.640
What did you call us?

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:41.140
Grucy!

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.140
You know, Gru and Lucy mushed together.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:44.060
Try it!

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.440
I like it, but not a lot.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.220
I don't like it.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.210
Huh?

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:06.430
Gru?

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:07.730
We can make it!

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:14.210
We can make it!

00:05:14.211 --> 00:05:16.630
No, we can't!

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:20.620
Who's bad?

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:22.140
Get ready for-

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:35.000
Hey, how you doing?

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.140
Are you okay?

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.880
You guys are so cute.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:44.580
Go get him, Gru-Gru!

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:46.840
Hello, Gru.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.700
How's your transition coming?

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:53.220
You know, from world's worst villain to
world's worst agent?

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:54.560
Oh, that's hilarious.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:55.720
You should be on TV.

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:56.800
Oh, that's right!

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:57.700
You were!

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.460
But then you got cancelled!

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:02.960
What about that?

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:04.180
What?

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:05.640
Oh, corals!

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.120
Dance fight!

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:13.340
Die to be dead!

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.600
Die to be dead!

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:30.580
Alpha Team, the diamond is secure.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.080
Come and pick up the package.

00:06:32.081 --> 00:06:33.240
Copy that.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:34.380
Alpha Team, in approach.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:41.020
Gru!

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.820
Did you actually think I was unconscious?

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:46.040
It's called acting, Hoser.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.640
And clearly I've still got it!

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:06.540
I've been a bad boy!

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.720
Son of a... Betamax!

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:11.320
Go, go!

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:11.840
Get him!

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:12.360
Get him!

00:07:12.361 --> 00:07:13.420
He's getting away!

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:16.380
This isn't over, Gru.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:17.700
You hear me?

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:19.420
This is not over!

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:20.240
Yeah?

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:22.520
Well, I still have the diamond!

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:32.850
Happy birthday, dear Dan!

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:38.630
Happy birthday to you!

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:48.370
I

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:12.320
can't believe Brad got away again!

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:13.880
How is this possible?

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:15.500
How?

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:26.710
And it's not just that he got away,
it's that he's so smug about it!

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:29.570
I've been a bad boy!

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:30.650
Edna!

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:31.170
Hey!

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:32.450
Looking hot!

00:08:32.451 --> 00:08:33.451
Today.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:35.450
Got the cats on you.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:40.050
And it was so humiliating, dangling there
in the bubblegum speedo!

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:45.750
And I didn't have time to go to the gym
this week, and I had a big breakfast!

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:47.970
I was feeling a little bloated!

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.030
You know what?

00:08:51.031 --> 00:08:52.690
He's not even worth talking about.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:56.430
I don't even want to waste another breath
about the guy!

00:08:56.431 --> 00:08:58.390
And another thing!

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:03.230
Next time I see Brad, I will moonwalk all
over his stupid face!

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.970
Oh, despicable me.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:11.310
Thank you all for coming at such short
notice.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:16.062
It is with great sadness
that I inform you that

00:09:16.063 --> 00:09:20.650
as of today, I am retiring
as head of the AVL.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:23.490
Oh, no!

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:29.430
Your new leader is coming directly from
head office.

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:31.390
Effective immediately.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:39.150
She is the very gifted, very ambitious
Miss Valerie DaVinci.

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:46.070
As I look out over all your faces,
I am flooded with so many memories.

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:47.430
Oh, boy!

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:48.830
This is a snooze fest!

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.130
Blah, blah, blah!

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:50.810
We understand!

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:52.650
You're old, you're fat, you're dumb!

00:09:52.651 --> 00:09:54.690
Let me breathe in!

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.650
Oh, broke a little sweat there.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:01.370
First order of business.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.810
Which one of you losers is Agent Groove?

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:08.690
Oh, that would be me.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:12.870
Although, I don't know if I'd say loser,
per se.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.570
Kind of is...

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:18.290
Oh, it's the girls!

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:20.050
Not a good time!

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:21.330
Hey!

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:22.670
Yes, sir!

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.890
Ma'am, you're making me nervous.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:32.730
How could you let Balthazar Bratt, the
AVL's most wanted villain, just get away?

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:35.070
That is the opposite of what we do here!

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:36.930
Okay, okay, yes.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:38.710
Maybe he got away again.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:45.150
But he didn't get the diamond,
and I am this close to bringing him in.

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:46.630
This close!

00:10:46.631 --> 00:10:47.631
Ha!

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:49.170
Interesting.

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:50.630
You're fired!

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:51.690
What?

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.010
That's totally not fair!

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.570
Gru is a great agent!

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:56.950
This subtitle has been error.

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:06.450
Well, yes she did.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:14.550
Honey, you didn't have to do that.

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:16.190
I know how much you love your job.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:18.710
Well, I love other things more.

00:11:18.711 --> 00:11:23.550
You know, we're going to have to tell the
girls.

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:25.110
Can you do it?

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.570
The whole mom thing is still kind of new
to me.

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:29.710
Oh, sure.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:46.450
Hello?

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.270
This is unexpected.

00:12:03.271 --> 00:12:07.230
Well, you never got to go on a honeymoon,
so-We made you dinner!

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:08.430
It's a luau!

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:11.170
We got pineapples and coke and that's the
nuca lady!

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:12.810
Oh, yay!

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:30.310
The soup of the day, madame.

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:31.530
And monsieur?

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:33.450
The gummy bears were my idea.

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:41.100
Mmm, looks so good to even eat!

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:42.260
Am I right?

00:12:42.261 --> 00:12:45.380
But I made it for you.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:50.960
Good soup!

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:56.500
I love the combination of gummy bears with
meat!

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:06.060
I'm going to hold it in my mouth, because
it's so good I don't want to swallow it.

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:07.540
So, how was work?

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:09.560
Oh, did you take that guy down?

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.100
Did anything explode?

00:13:11.101 --> 00:13:20.560
Well, actually, today Lucy and I were
invited to not work at the ABL anymore.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:22.940
No!

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.280
You got fired?

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:28.820
Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:31.300
Yes.

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:33.480
But don't worry.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:36.260
I'm sure we'll get new jobs real soon.

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:38.080
Even better ones.

00:13:38.081 --> 00:13:41.840
What's better than being super cool secret
agents?

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:44.380
Oh, I know.

00:13:44.381 --> 00:13:45.800
You can gamble online.

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:47.620
That's what Katie's dad does.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:51.020
Okay, we will definitely look into that.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:52.420
That's a good suggestion.

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:56.200
And let's not go over to Katie's house
anymore.

00:13:58.740 --> 00:13:59.740
Hmm?

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:05.900
Guys, I don't think you've heard me right.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:06.960
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:09.660
This does not mean that we are going back
to being villains.

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:12.760
Pinyu, flacomico!

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:14.120
Okay, all right.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.040
I get it.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:17.580
Look, I know it's been a little tough
lately.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:22.920
Especially with Dr. Nefario accidentally
freezing himself in carbonite.

00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:29.320
But our life of crime is over.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:33.740
Now, now, you're with me on this,
right?

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:54.740
Guys, listen to me.

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:55.880
Read my lips.

00:14:55.881 --> 00:14:57.980
Listen me lipo.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.180
Pomodoro wacomquit.

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:05.500
What did I say?

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:06.800
It's not comquit?

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:08.920
Oh, okay.

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:10.580
Pomodoro wacomquit.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:15.400
Don't take the tongue with me.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:17.500
We're not going back to villainy.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:22.000
Yes, and I don't want to hear another word
about it.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:30.280
Look, if you guys don't stop right now,
there will be consequences.

00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:35.120
Hey, don't say anything you're going to
regret.

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:43.200
You're serious?

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:44.180
Come on.

00:15:44.181 --> 00:15:46.380
No, no, no, no, no.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:49.920
Pudgy?

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:51.460
Hey, Jerry!

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.360
Great news, guys.

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:56.280
You have been promoted.

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:57.540
You're in charge now.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.500
Not bad.

00:16:01.710 --> 00:16:02.370
Yee-bah!

00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:03.230
Yee-bah!

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:04.230
Yee-bah!

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:06.910
Rooba, Rooba, Rooba, Rooba, Rooba,
Rooba!

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:09.650
Jish!

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:33.080
Ah, Monsieur Pompe,
to what do we owe the

00:16:33.081 --> 00:16:37.781
presence of the world's
foremost gem expert?

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:39.560
The chief of police sent me.

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:42.072
He was concerned that
during the recent heist

00:16:42.073 --> 00:16:46.140
attempt, the Dumont diamond
was replaced with a phony.

00:16:46.141 --> 00:16:47.141
Huh?

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:07.640
Now, you have been duped.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:08.440
What?

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:09.320
We have?

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:10.600
Yes.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:11.900
By me!

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:18.740
But what is...

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:31.673
Oh, should I say.

00:17:45.683 --> 00:17:45.230
..

00:17:45.231 --> 00:17:47.490
Je suis ce mauvais gosseau!

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:02.920
No!

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:27.230
Hey, girl.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.150
What you doing down here?

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:30.670
In the dark?

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:31.870
Alone?

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:33.350
Oh, nothing.

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:34.370
Just thinking.

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:36.310
You okay?

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:37.390
Oh, yes.

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:38.270
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:39.110
I'm fine.

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:42.370
It's just... Ah, I don't know.

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:46.230
I guess I just feel like a failure.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:49.310
Like I don't have a purpose anymore.

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:52.350
Hey, Mister, you are not a failure.

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:55.690
If only I could have nailed Brad.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:59.690
So many times I almost had him.

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:04.590
But now I'll never get the chance,
because I have been kicked to the curb.

00:19:04.591 --> 00:19:06.370
Gru, you've got to let this go.

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:07.770
It's time to look forward.

00:19:08.610 --> 00:19:10.730
Things will get better, I promise.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:29.260
Excuse me.

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:32.540
Pardon me, young people.

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:35.740
Would you tell me how to get to this
address?

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:42.120
I'm looking for a Mr. Gru.

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:57.790
Idiots.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:00.850
No!

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:01.530
Kyle!

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:02.230
Stop!

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:03.930
Kyle, let go!

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:09.630
No, no!

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:11.110
You've got to be kidding me!

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.890
Lucy, did you see... He helps
you if you have nightmare.

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:16.530
And he's really good to snuggle with.

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:17.470
Oh, no, no, no.

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:18.290
Agnes, Agnes!

00:20:18.291 --> 00:20:18.330
No.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:20.430
Take good care of him.

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:21.750
Thank you!

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:23.750
Agnes, what are you doing?

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:26.450
You sold your unicorn?

00:20:27.010 --> 00:20:30.290
I just wanted to help, since you don't
have a job.

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:33.710
I got two whole dollars for it.

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:38.150
Excuse me.

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:40.070
Sorry, buddy, the sale's over.

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.450
Yes, but this will
only take a... Hey!

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:43.330
Eyebrows!

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:44.450
Get off the lawn!

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:48.850
Yeah, but... Hey, could
you... Oh, of course.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:51.070
Now, as I was saying...

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:53.370
Oh, goodbye!

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:02.340
Listen, Agnes, you don't need to worry.

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:03.920
We're going to be fine.

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:04.860
For real?

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.200
For real.

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:08.280
Now, come on, let's pack this stuff up.

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:10.640
Seriously?

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:12.900
Buddy, you're not getting the...

00:21:12.901 --> 00:21:18.900
Excuse me, Mr. Groove, but I really must
have a word with you.

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:20.360
How do you know my name?

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:22.480
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:24.100
My name is Groove.

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:25.460
Ow!

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:26.900
Good puppy!

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:31.700
And I am inquiring on behalf of your twin
brother, Groove.

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:33.340
He needs your help.

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:34.160
What?

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:35.240
Twin brother?

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:36.360
Twin brother?

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:37.080
Big brother?

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:38.200
Oh, yeah.

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:41.380
He would like to fly you to Fredonia to
meet him.

00:21:41.381 --> 00:21:46.820
Your father has recently passed
away, and... Oh, okay, Coco.

00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:49.800
I'm sorry, but my dad died when I was a
baby.

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:51.360
And I don't have any brother.

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:52.540
You got the wrong guy.

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:53.720
Really?

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:57.640
Well, then, how do you explain this?

00:21:58.260 --> 00:21:59.260
You what?

00:22:03.690 --> 00:22:05.310
Ha ha ha!

00:22:05.830 --> 00:22:06.830
Bellissimo!

00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:10.530
Oh, hello, Groove.

00:22:10.690 --> 00:22:11.510
Hi, Mom.

00:22:11.511 --> 00:22:15.750
It's important to keep active in one's
golden years.

00:22:17.090 --> 00:22:19.790
There you are, you cutie!

00:22:23.250 --> 00:22:28.510
These are my diving instructors,
Vincenzo and Paolo.

00:22:30.550 --> 00:22:31.870
Ciao, boys.

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:34.570
So, what do you want?

00:22:35.190 --> 00:22:37.770
Mom, do I have a twin brother?

00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:40.310
How did you find out?

00:22:40.370 --> 00:22:41.250
Who told you?

00:22:41.251 --> 00:22:41.770
Wait, what?

00:22:41.810 --> 00:22:42.510
It's true!

00:22:42.790 --> 00:22:44.530
You never told me I had a brother!

00:22:44.850 --> 00:22:48.170
And you told me that dad died of
disappointment when I was born!

00:22:48.550 --> 00:22:49.550
Yeah, yeah.

00:22:49.790 --> 00:22:51.490
That was the agreement.

00:22:52.130 --> 00:22:52.690
Agreement?

00:22:53.090 --> 00:22:54.670
What are you talking about?

00:22:57.810 --> 00:23:02.910
Shortly after you and your brother were
born, your father and I divorced.

00:23:03.470 --> 00:23:10.371
We each took one son to raise on our own
and promised never to see each other again.

00:23:12.930 --> 00:23:15.630
Obviously, I got second pick.

00:23:18.770 --> 00:23:20.130
I have a brother.

00:23:27.270 --> 00:23:28.290
Hey, girls!

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:30.270
How are things in row B, huh?

00:23:30.530 --> 00:23:32.550
I put together some fun activities for the
trip.

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:35.370
Who is up for some gin rummy?

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.430
Yeah, um, we're good.

00:23:39.431 --> 00:23:41.070
Oh, okay.

00:23:42.030 --> 00:23:43.730
I'll just sit here and play solitaire.

00:23:44.610 --> 00:23:45.670
I hope I win.

00:23:47.050 --> 00:23:48.630
I wonder what the row will be like.

00:23:49.230 --> 00:23:53.170
Maybe we'll have the twin thing when you
can read each other's minds.

00:23:53.650 --> 00:23:53.970
No?

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:55.510
How cool would that be?

00:23:55.690 --> 00:23:57.090
Um, super cool.

00:24:26.500 --> 00:24:29.720
I can't wait to meet my brother!

00:24:30.900 --> 00:24:32.620
What's with all the pigs?

00:24:33.040 --> 00:24:35.040
This is the family business.

00:24:35.460 --> 00:24:38.560
The largest pig farm in the whole of
Fredonia.

00:24:40.040 --> 00:24:41.420
Okay, nice pig.

00:24:41.880 --> 00:24:44.640
Now, that's my private part.

00:24:47.720 --> 00:24:49.280
This pig has issues!

00:24:50.440 --> 00:24:51.920
Please, come in.

00:24:51.921 --> 00:24:52.921
Blah!

00:24:53.760 --> 00:24:54.800
Oh,

00:25:02.840 --> 00:25:04.300
this is amazing!

00:25:05.160 --> 00:25:06.640
It's like the Sistine Chapel!

00:25:07.180 --> 00:25:09.400
But with pigs...

00:25:20.970 --> 00:25:21.970
My brother!

00:25:27.670 --> 00:25:31.170
Brother, I am so happy!

00:25:34.930 --> 00:25:38.570
After all of these years, finally I'm
meeting you!

00:25:38.630 --> 00:25:40.310
Yup, alright, cut!

00:25:40.910 --> 00:25:42.510
Oh, look at that!

00:25:43.010 --> 00:25:45.150
You must be the beautiful wife!

00:25:45.370 --> 00:25:46.370
Beautiful?

00:25:46.590 --> 00:25:47.790
Oh, that's a dog!

00:25:48.510 --> 00:25:49.290
Sweet talker.

00:25:49.390 --> 00:25:52.450
How is my brother finding a wife like you
when he is so bald?

00:25:53.730 --> 00:25:54.730
I'm joking!

00:25:56.950 --> 00:26:00.050
This must be my nieces!

00:26:01.110 --> 00:26:01.770
You're Agnes!

00:26:02.050 --> 00:26:04.270
You are small with big eyes!

00:26:04.271 --> 00:26:06.470
And it makes me want to put you in my
pocket!

00:26:06.650 --> 00:26:08.130
You can't do that!

00:26:08.410 --> 00:26:09.890
I'm too big!

00:26:10.590 --> 00:26:11.230
He did!

00:26:11.510 --> 00:26:14.950
I can tell that you are a little
mischievous!

00:26:15.030 --> 00:26:17.310
We're going to have to make a little
trouble later.

00:26:17.610 --> 00:26:17.870
What?

00:26:17.970 --> 00:26:18.970
I already have!

00:26:19.570 --> 00:26:19.570
Ow!

00:26:20.230 --> 00:26:20.230
Ow!

00:26:20.850 --> 00:26:20.850
Ow!

00:26:21.010 --> 00:26:22.010
Please!

00:26:24.740 --> 00:26:27.700
This must be mischievous behavior!

00:26:28.580 --> 00:26:32.140
And Margo, oh, you are so mature,
I'm guessing.

00:26:32.460 --> 00:26:33.820
Why, are you fifteen?

00:26:34.700 --> 00:26:35.360
Fifteen?

00:26:35.361 --> 00:26:36.480
She's twelve.

00:26:36.700 --> 00:26:39.060
She looks twelve and will always be
twelve.

00:26:39.580 --> 00:26:42.340
So, Drew, this place is amazing!

00:26:42.520 --> 00:26:44.800
I mean, you just walk through the doors
and you're like...

00:26:46.920 --> 00:26:48.720
It's nice, I guess, sure.

00:26:48.940 --> 00:26:50.360
I'm not really into things.

00:27:01.360 --> 00:27:03.020
Yes, the best!

00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:04.360
Alright, let's go home now.

00:27:04.380 --> 00:27:04.760
Home?

00:27:04.880 --> 00:27:05.340
Why?

00:27:05.341 --> 00:27:06.341
I don't know.

00:27:06.500 --> 00:27:09.599
This guy with the mansion
and the cars and all

00:27:09.600 --> 00:27:13.720
the hair with the silky
smooth luxurious hair.

00:27:13.900 --> 00:27:16.260
I feel worse than I did before I came.

00:27:16.700 --> 00:27:18.020
He's your brother, Drew.

00:27:18.320 --> 00:27:19.240
Give this a chance.

00:27:19.300 --> 00:27:22.087
Oh, I was thinking while
Drew and I catch up on some

00:27:22.088 --> 00:27:24.380
brother stuff, you girls
should go with friends.

00:27:24.560 --> 00:27:25.680
He has a surprise for you.

00:27:25.780 --> 00:27:26.260
Yay!

00:27:26.440 --> 00:27:26.800
Awesome!

00:27:26.900 --> 00:27:28.000
I love surprises!

00:27:28.280 --> 00:27:29.280
Oh, this is perfect!

00:27:29.380 --> 00:27:30.436
Mother-daughter bonding time.

00:27:30.460 --> 00:27:31.460
Let's do it!

00:27:31.980 --> 00:27:32.980
Bye!

00:27:33.640 --> 00:27:34.640
You boys have fun!

00:27:36.620 --> 00:27:37.620
Whoopee!

00:27:40.880 --> 00:27:44.473
Now you can be as evil as
Balthazar Brat with the Evil Brat

00:27:44.474 --> 00:27:48.780
action figure featuring
music-activated break-dance mode.

00:27:49.440 --> 00:27:52.600
Also featuring bubblegum-launching
shoulder pads.

00:27:53.780 --> 00:27:56.580
And the all-new Mega Diamond Laser!

00:27:59.180 --> 00:28:00.600
No more masks!

00:28:00.980 --> 00:28:03.060
I've been a bad boy!

00:28:04.160 --> 00:28:07.300
Mega Diamond Laser does not actually
incinerate books.

00:28:07.940 --> 00:28:12.780
How could Hollywood cancel a show that
produced toys like this, Clive?

00:28:13.920 --> 00:28:15.900
Evil Brat was a masterpiece!

00:28:16.300 --> 00:28:18.640
Does no one value true art anymore?

00:28:18.840 --> 00:28:20.820
It's a disgrace and a travesty,
sir.

00:28:21.140 --> 00:28:24.600
Well, now that I've got the diamond,
it's payback time.

00:28:25.120 --> 00:28:28.460
Oh, it's too bad Gru won't be around to
try and stop me.

00:28:28.940 --> 00:28:29.320
Oh, wait!

00:28:29.321 --> 00:28:29.900
No, it's not!

00:28:30.040 --> 00:28:31.300
I hate that dweeb!

00:28:31.301 --> 00:28:33.000
And you, Hollywood!

00:28:33.520 --> 00:28:39.700
This time, I'm canceling you and all the
losers who rejected me!

00:28:44.900 --> 00:28:50.380
So, how are things going for you
career-wise?

00:28:51.200 --> 00:28:52.200
Great!

00:28:52.480 --> 00:28:53.560
So, so great!

00:28:54.240 --> 00:28:55.240
Crushing it!

00:28:55.380 --> 00:29:00.340
Well, I've got something that I think
you'll find very interesting.

00:29:02.800 --> 00:29:05.080
Hold on to your face, brother!

00:29:38.700 --> 00:29:41.400
What is all this?

00:29:41.780 --> 00:29:45.660
The pig farm was just a cover for the real
family business.

00:29:47.020 --> 00:29:48.020
Oh!

00:29:48.740 --> 00:29:50.880
Hey, it's Gru with boobs!

00:29:52.660 --> 00:29:55.660
Now, feast your eyes on...

00:29:57.980 --> 00:29:59.580
Dad's Lair!

00:29:59.980 --> 00:30:00.980
Ta-da!

00:30:02.120 --> 00:30:04.140
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:30:04.220 --> 00:30:07.200
Wait, so our dad was a villain?

00:30:07.820 --> 00:30:08.480
No, no, no!

00:30:08.481 --> 00:30:13.120
Not just a villain, but one of the
greatest of all time!

00:30:13.121 --> 00:30:17.340
He was known as the Bald Terror!

00:30:18.280 --> 00:30:19.340
That's him?

00:30:20.260 --> 00:30:21.260
Our dad?

00:30:21.300 --> 00:30:24.640
He was so proud of you and what a great
villain you were!

00:30:25.620 --> 00:30:26.620
He was?

00:30:26.680 --> 00:30:27.680
For me?

00:30:28.480 --> 00:30:29.920
Not so much.

00:30:30.280 --> 00:30:34.760
To dad, I was just a failure.

00:30:36.080 --> 00:30:38.200
Never thought I had what it took to be a
villain.

00:30:39.020 --> 00:30:41.740
But now you can help me prove him wrong!

00:30:42.540 --> 00:30:46.740
Brother, teach me the art of villainy!

00:30:49.040 --> 00:30:51.240
No, no, no, no.

00:30:51.241 --> 00:30:52.241
I can't do that.

00:30:52.360 --> 00:30:52.780
What?

00:30:52.860 --> 00:30:55.020
But it's our family tradition!

00:30:55.140 --> 00:30:56.600
You can't say no to that!

00:30:57.340 --> 00:30:58.520
Look, I'm sorry.

00:30:58.860 --> 00:31:00.720
I left that life behind me.

00:31:00.960 --> 00:31:01.960
End of story.

00:31:02.940 --> 00:31:05.960
Oh... Okay, I understand.

00:31:06.800 --> 00:31:08.560
I wonder what this does.

00:31:11.740 --> 00:31:13.620
No, no, no, no!

00:31:25.720 --> 00:31:27.240
Holy moly!

00:31:27.460 --> 00:31:29.160
Dad's villain wheels!

00:31:29.760 --> 00:31:30.760
Pretty slick!

00:31:31.760 --> 00:31:34.620
Hey, you wanna take her out for a spin?

00:31:34.640 --> 00:31:35.940
Just for some fun?

00:31:51.540 --> 00:31:54.260
Zero to 403 seconds!

00:31:54.300 --> 00:31:56.320
Able to withstand a nuclear blast!

00:31:56.580 --> 00:31:57.720
I'm to the D!

00:31:57.721 --> 00:32:02.200
Oh, yeah, that's pretty nice!

00:32:02.340 --> 00:32:03.840
And it's a hybrid!

00:32:04.140 --> 00:32:05.140
Look out!

00:32:27.610 --> 00:32:29.030
Help me!

00:32:31.430 --> 00:32:34.690
I am not enjoying this!

00:32:40.160 --> 00:32:41.400
Wow,

00:32:45.140 --> 00:32:46.540
what is going on here?

00:32:46.541 --> 00:32:50.560
Welcome to the annual Fredonian Cheese
Festival!

00:32:51.120 --> 00:32:52.120
Go!

00:33:02.650 --> 00:33:04.710
Lucy, can we get these, please?

00:33:05.270 --> 00:33:07.130
Okay, but only one each.

00:33:07.250 --> 00:33:08.250
I mean it.

00:33:08.710 --> 00:33:09.710
Aw, man!

00:33:10.190 --> 00:33:10.770
No, I don't.

00:33:11.170 --> 00:33:12.170
Get as many as you want.

00:33:12.390 --> 00:33:13.390
I don't care.

00:33:13.510 --> 00:33:13.970
Yay!

00:33:14.230 --> 00:33:15.230
Awesome!

00:33:15.470 --> 00:33:16.390
Uh... What?

00:33:16.790 --> 00:33:18.950
Well, it's okay to tell them no.

00:33:19.150 --> 00:33:19.990
Sometimes, too.

00:33:20.170 --> 00:33:20.490
You know?

00:33:20.850 --> 00:33:21.910
Moms need to be tough.

00:33:22.390 --> 00:33:23.410
Right, right.

00:33:23.411 --> 00:33:23.750
Tough.

00:33:23.870 --> 00:33:24.290
Good one.

00:33:24.330 --> 00:33:25.510
I can totally do that.

00:33:25.511 --> 00:33:27.710
You know, still figuring out this mom
thing.

00:33:27.930 --> 00:33:29.050
Getting my silly legs.

00:33:29.270 --> 00:33:30.270
Maybe.

00:33:30.710 --> 00:33:31.830
It's a unicorn!

00:33:42.580 --> 00:33:44.760
Um, sure, yeah.

00:33:44.880 --> 00:33:47.761
But first, let's,
um... Oh, look!

00:33:48.340 --> 00:33:50.320
It's a traditional Fredonian dance.

00:33:50.460 --> 00:33:52.020
How amazing does that look?

00:33:52.420 --> 00:33:54.080
Say Say Say Cheese!

00:33:55.140 --> 00:33:56.140
Cheese!

00:33:56.240 --> 00:33:57.240
I love this.

00:33:58.280 --> 00:34:00.800
The little girls go and get the cheese
from the little boys?

00:34:00.801 --> 00:34:02.300
That's adorable!

00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:07.200
Aw, look at that poor little guy.

00:34:07.700 --> 00:34:08.740
With his little boots.

00:34:09.620 --> 00:34:10.720
Nobody picked him.

00:34:11.580 --> 00:34:12.200
Oh, Marco.

00:34:12.580 --> 00:34:13.720
Why don't you go up there?

00:34:13.920 --> 00:34:14.920
No way.

00:34:15.080 --> 00:34:16.080
Okay.

00:34:16.600 --> 00:34:17.600
Wait a minute.

00:34:17.720 --> 00:34:18.040
No.

00:34:18.740 --> 00:34:22.020
Go take a bite of his cheese, young lady,
right now.

00:34:22.580 --> 00:34:23.000
What?

00:34:23.360 --> 00:34:24.100
I'm being tougher.

00:34:24.300 --> 00:34:25.320
You know, like you said.

00:34:25.580 --> 00:34:27.700
No, I meant be tougher on them.

00:34:27.960 --> 00:34:28.540
Not me.

00:34:28.541 --> 00:34:29.440
Oh, come on.

00:34:29.441 --> 00:34:30.120
Just do it.

00:34:30.220 --> 00:34:31.800
What's the worst that could happen?

00:34:34.940 --> 00:34:35.940
Fine.

00:34:42.460 --> 00:34:43.620
Hey there.

00:34:43.880 --> 00:34:44.880
I'm Margo.

00:34:45.600 --> 00:34:46.760
Hello, Margo.

00:34:47.320 --> 00:34:48.580
I am Nico.

00:34:48.980 --> 00:34:50.700
Would you like some of my cheese?

00:34:53.680 --> 00:34:55.180
Yes, yes, yes.

00:34:55.181 --> 00:34:56.181
Thank you, Margo.

00:34:56.220 --> 00:34:57.220
Thank you.

00:34:58.720 --> 00:35:01.180
Hey, I am a great mother.

00:35:01.181 --> 00:35:02.460
Do you see that, girls?

00:35:02.980 --> 00:35:06.720
I laid down the...
Where are they?

00:35:07.540 --> 00:35:08.540
Oh, Agnes.

00:35:09.080 --> 00:35:10.080
Edith.

00:35:13.010 --> 00:35:14.010
Hello.

00:35:16.970 --> 00:35:17.690
Look!

00:35:17.830 --> 00:35:19.030
A unicorn horn!

00:35:21.940 --> 00:35:24.220
My little brain is going to explode!

00:35:25.340 --> 00:35:27.020
Agnes, that's fake.

00:35:27.620 --> 00:35:30.360
Oh, it's real, all right.

00:35:30.361 --> 00:35:34.420
That horn came from the crooked forest.

00:35:34.860 --> 00:35:39.500
The only place on earth where unicorns
still live.

00:35:46.540 --> 00:35:47.860
Laugh, laugh, all of you!

00:35:48.740 --> 00:35:50.560
They all think I'm crazy.

00:35:51.240 --> 00:35:56.300
But I'm telling you, I saw one once with
my own eye.

00:35:56.301 --> 00:35:57.440
Whoa, wait.

00:35:57.660 --> 00:35:59.520
You saw a for real-life unicorn?

00:36:00.140 --> 00:36:01.140
What did it look like?

00:36:01.420 --> 00:36:02.200
Did you pet it?

00:36:02.300 --> 00:36:03.300
Did it smell like candy?

00:36:05.460 --> 00:36:06.460
What?

00:36:06.580 --> 00:36:08.020
It was so fluffy.

00:36:08.940 --> 00:36:11.060
I thought I was going to die.

00:36:12.120 --> 00:36:13.800
Do you think maybe I could find one too?

00:36:14.240 --> 00:36:17.880
Oh, they say if a maiden
pure of heart goes into the

00:36:17.881 --> 00:36:24.720
crooked forest, the unicorn
will come and be hers forever.

00:36:32.400 --> 00:36:33.400
Agnes!

00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:45.990
Are you okay?

00:36:47.070 --> 00:36:48.150
Yeah, we're fine.

00:36:48.890 --> 00:36:49.890
Are you?

00:36:50.310 --> 00:36:51.590
Unicorns are really real!

00:36:51.870 --> 00:36:53.490
And I'm going to find one!

00:36:56.460 --> 00:36:59.100
Sorry, went a little mama bear on you.

00:36:59.260 --> 00:37:02.401
You know, I heard a scream
and... Yeah, okay, have a good one.

00:37:07.210 --> 00:37:08.450
Wait for me here.

00:37:08.650 --> 00:37:08.870
Don't!

00:37:09.250 --> 00:37:10.250
Stop that!

00:37:10.670 --> 00:37:11.970
You'll kick me!

00:37:13.870 --> 00:37:14.870
Hey, hey!

00:37:15.070 --> 00:37:16.070
What are you doing?

00:37:16.930 --> 00:37:18.850
Did you just steal candies?

00:37:19.030 --> 00:37:19.470
Yes!

00:37:19.750 --> 00:37:22.570
That's a lot of effort for two lollipops.

00:37:23.990 --> 00:37:24.990
Snocky!

00:37:27.570 --> 00:37:28.570
Oh, no!

00:37:28.670 --> 00:37:29.230
The police!

00:37:29.410 --> 00:37:29.870
What do we do?

00:37:29.970 --> 00:37:30.970
What do we do?

00:37:31.110 --> 00:37:31.870
Come on!

00:37:32.030 --> 00:37:33.830
This is going to be fun!

00:37:43.290 --> 00:37:45.390
The police are going to get us!

00:37:46.010 --> 00:37:47.010
Bring it out!

00:37:47.730 --> 00:37:48.730
Pigs!

00:37:51.060 --> 00:37:51.600
Cops!

00:37:51.860 --> 00:37:52.980
Take him with us!

00:38:03.520 --> 00:38:04.520
Whoa!

00:38:08.600 --> 00:38:09.600
They're back!

00:38:11.710 --> 00:38:12.710
Yeah!

00:38:33.800 --> 00:38:35.820
Man, that was crazy!

00:38:36.380 --> 00:38:37.960
We're so close to getting busted!

00:38:38.220 --> 00:38:39.160
Tell me about it.

00:38:39.220 --> 00:38:41.120
I thought you were going to pee your
pants!

00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:43.000
I did!

00:38:43.320 --> 00:38:44.320
You did!

00:38:51.590 --> 00:38:52.630
Mel, poof!

00:38:55.770 --> 00:38:56.770
Hey, Mel!

00:38:56.830 --> 00:38:57.270
The mastic!

00:38:57.530 --> 00:38:58.090
The papaya!

00:38:58.130 --> 00:38:58.670
Not the potato!

00:38:58.910 --> 00:38:59.910
Hey, the potato!

00:39:01.190 --> 00:39:01.910
The pizza!

00:39:02.110 --> 00:39:02.510
Not to eat!

00:39:02.511 --> 00:39:03.630
We're going to eat it all!

00:39:34.080 --> 00:39:34.800
Come on!

00:39:34.940 --> 00:39:35.320
Come on!

00:39:35.440 --> 00:39:35.820
Tempura!

00:39:36.060 --> 00:39:37.060
Carbonara!

00:39:39.280 --> 00:39:40.280
Hey, hey, hey!

00:39:41.220 --> 00:39:53.390
Hey, hey, hey!

00:40:14.620 --> 00:40:15.820
Papama Luka!

00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:16.180
Pippa!

00:40:16.320 --> 00:40:16.660
Roo!

00:40:16.840 --> 00:40:17.840
Pippa!

00:40:18.520 --> 00:40:19.520
Pippa!

00:40:30.380 --> 00:40:31.380
Pippa!

00:40:35.520 --> 00:40:35.720
Pippa!

00:40:35.721 --> 00:40:36.721
Get him!

00:40:37.640 --> 00:40:38.640
Go, go!

00:40:40.740 --> 00:40:41.740
Pippa!

00:40:41.880 --> 00:40:42.880
Pippa!

00:40:52.830 --> 00:40:53.830
Pippa!

00:41:19.190 --> 00:41:21.190
Hands in the air!

00:41:29.410 --> 00:41:31.910
Face it, Gru, villainy is in your blood!

00:41:32.990 --> 00:41:35.490
You can't tell me you don't miss the rush
a little.

00:41:37.150 --> 00:41:38.510
Maybe a little.

00:41:38.970 --> 00:41:44.470
And now you got the chance to get back on
top, get your mojo back, become Gru again.

00:41:44.730 --> 00:41:46.450
How awesome would that be?

00:41:48.870 --> 00:41:50.870
Oh, please, come on.

00:41:51.030 --> 00:41:52.490
Just one heist.

00:41:53.490 --> 00:41:59.530
There's got to be something out there
somewhere that you still want to steal.

00:42:03.410 --> 00:42:05.170
There is something.

00:42:05.790 --> 00:42:11.830
How about we steal the largest diamond in
the world?

00:42:12.250 --> 00:42:12.710
Yes!

00:42:12.930 --> 00:42:14.330
I love it!

00:42:15.410 --> 00:42:16.650
Thank you, brother.

00:42:16.810 --> 00:42:19.290
Thank you from the bottom of my heart.

00:42:21.830 --> 00:42:22.810
You know what?

00:42:22.811 --> 00:42:24.570
We should do something to celebrate.

00:42:26.530 --> 00:42:28.710
I've got the perfect idea.

00:42:32.410 --> 00:42:35.210
Fritz, my good fellow, could you get me
another napkin, please?

00:42:35.410 --> 00:42:37.210
I guess, of course, Miss Eden.

00:42:44.500 --> 00:42:45.860
Hey, we're a Gru and Drew.

00:42:46.460 --> 00:42:47.960
Here we are!

00:42:48.840 --> 00:42:49.960
How's it going?

00:42:51.540 --> 00:42:53.320
It's me, Gru.

00:42:53.580 --> 00:42:55.200
And me, Drew.

00:42:56.340 --> 00:43:00.020
I hug everybody whether they like it or
not.

00:43:00.560 --> 00:43:02.440
Why are they pretending to be each other?

00:43:03.760 --> 00:43:07.860
Oh, that's for dinner, but probably won't
like it.

00:43:08.060 --> 00:43:10.340
I'm so grumpy all the time.

00:43:11.000 --> 00:43:15.100
Hey, I laugh a lot, and I'm kind of an
idiot.

00:43:21.040 --> 00:43:22.540
Woo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

00:43:25.800 --> 00:43:27.320
I'm busted in the gut.

00:43:27.680 --> 00:43:28.920
Look at them!

00:43:29.240 --> 00:43:33.210
They are total barns.

00:43:33.211 --> 00:43:34.930
Oh, look, it's me, Gru.

00:43:35.390 --> 00:43:36.490
And I'm Drew.

00:43:36.650 --> 00:43:38.070
We switched places.

00:43:38.790 --> 00:43:41.030
Oh, it's so nice to see you two are
getting along.

00:43:41.570 --> 00:43:43.750
We are getting along perfectly.

00:43:44.890 --> 00:43:47.930
Wait, did we just finish each other's
sentences?

00:43:49.510 --> 00:43:51.010
Oh, that's delightful.

00:43:51.130 --> 00:43:52.090
Not creepy at all.

00:43:52.091 --> 00:43:53.810
And you're going to stop now though,
right?

00:43:53.870 --> 00:43:55.850
Sorry, it's a twin thing.

00:43:56.410 --> 00:43:57.410
Uh-huh.

00:43:57.910 --> 00:44:00.790
So, what did you guys do today?

00:44:01.770 --> 00:44:02.770
Nothing.

00:44:03.810 --> 00:44:04.810
Okay, what does it say?

00:44:04.850 --> 00:44:05.850
All done.

00:44:06.830 --> 00:44:07.510
Pardon me.

00:44:07.850 --> 00:44:09.270
Good night, everybody.

00:44:09.390 --> 00:44:11.370
Hey, hey, hey, put the brakes on.

00:44:11.430 --> 00:44:12.090
What's the rush?

00:44:12.190 --> 00:44:14.710
I need to get to bed so I can wake up and
find a unicorn.

00:44:15.010 --> 00:44:16.010
Good night.

00:44:17.970 --> 00:44:19.150
What was that about?

00:44:19.151 --> 00:44:22.830
Agnes thinks she's going to find a real
unicorn in the woods tomorrow.

00:44:23.530 --> 00:44:25.090
She's totally freaking out.

00:44:25.410 --> 00:44:27.410
I feel like someone's got to tell her the
truth.

00:44:28.150 --> 00:44:29.150
Not it.

00:44:29.590 --> 00:44:32.370
Oh, don't worry, parenting 101.

00:44:32.690 --> 00:44:33.690
I get this.

00:44:36.650 --> 00:44:40.810
And please bless that when I find a
unicorn, he'll want to come home with me.

00:44:40.990 --> 00:44:44.450
And sleep in my room so that I can ride
him to school every day.

00:44:45.490 --> 00:44:48.330
And he'll use his magical powers to help
me do math.

00:44:49.470 --> 00:44:50.470
Amen.

00:44:55.610 --> 00:44:56.750
Hey, Xo.

00:44:57.350 --> 00:44:58.770
Big day tomorrow.

00:44:59.330 --> 00:45:03.450
Yeah, I'm finally going to get to see a
unicorn for reals.

00:45:03.570 --> 00:45:05.470
If I do, can I bring it home?

00:45:06.210 --> 00:45:06.430
Please.

00:45:07.210 --> 00:45:08.930
Oh, yeah, sure.

00:45:09.170 --> 00:45:13.370
Tell you what, every unicorn you find,
you can bring it home.

00:45:13.850 --> 00:45:16.370
I better build a big pet, right?

00:45:17.570 --> 00:45:23.050
But, you know... There's a
chance that you might not find one.

00:45:24.010 --> 00:45:25.010
Huh?

00:45:26.790 --> 00:45:31.210
It might not be good unicorn finding
weather.

00:45:33.710 --> 00:45:37.250
Um, they're tricky to find them.

00:45:38.250 --> 00:45:41.010
And, I don't know, maybe...

00:45:42.830 --> 00:45:43.830
Maybe...

00:45:44.510 --> 00:45:47.010
Unicorns don't really...

00:45:50.870 --> 00:45:53.930
...explore that part of the woods.

00:45:57.010 --> 00:46:01.930
But the man said a maiden could find one
if she was pure in heart.

00:46:02.330 --> 00:46:04.190
I'm pure in heart, right?

00:46:06.230 --> 00:46:07.430
The purest.

00:46:11.590 --> 00:46:13.490
Can we stop talking now?

00:46:13.690 --> 00:46:14.870
I need to get to sleep.

00:46:14.871 --> 00:46:16.410
Good night, sweetie.

00:46:16.990 --> 00:46:17.990
Good night, girl.

00:46:28.450 --> 00:46:29.810
I'm okay!

00:46:33.690 --> 00:46:34.870
Hold on to me...

00:46:38.970 --> 00:46:39.710
You can't really see... Hey!

00:46:39.730 --> 00:46:40.730
Get that back!

00:46:41.210 --> 00:46:43.910
You can't really see...
You can't really see!

00:46:43.911 --> 00:46:44.930
You can't really see!

00:47:11.910 --> 00:47:15.070
We've been waiting a long time.

00:47:15.071 --> 00:47:17.570
Can we... No, no, no!

00:48:21.650 --> 00:48:26.010
Because I'm training for the big day.

00:48:26.250 --> 00:48:28.390
Nobody's gonna stop me.

00:48:28.391 --> 00:48:33.290
Because I am super-sassy, super-sassy,
super-sassy.

00:48:34.350 --> 00:48:36.270
What's today's plan, boss?

00:48:36.430 --> 00:48:37.690
What's the plan?

00:48:38.370 --> 00:48:40.510
Silly robot, I'll show you the plan.

00:48:40.730 --> 00:48:43.690
Time to watch a very special episode of
Evil Brat.

00:48:43.850 --> 00:48:47.030
To see exactly what I'm gonna do to stupid
Tensel Town.

00:48:48.530 --> 00:48:51.330
This week on Evil Brat!

00:48:53.370 --> 00:48:56.010
It's a giant Evil Brat robot!

00:48:56.011 --> 00:48:58.010
Open fire!

00:49:03.630 --> 00:49:04.830
Nice try, coppers.

00:49:05.130 --> 00:49:06.170
Chew on this!

00:49:08.770 --> 00:49:12.750
He's shooting his super-sticky,
self-inflating gum!

00:49:13.950 --> 00:49:14.950
Run!

00:49:15.790 --> 00:49:17.790
Gum won, gum all!

00:49:19.870 --> 00:49:21.530
Gum won, gum all.

00:49:21.810 --> 00:49:24.490
Seriously, how did this show never win an
Emmy?

00:49:27.010 --> 00:49:31.310
And now, it's your turn to shine,
my diamond!

00:49:43.470 --> 00:49:48.050
Hey, Clive, I guess you could say our plan
was out of this world.

00:49:52.550 --> 00:49:54.550
Now that's entertainment!

00:49:55.050 --> 00:49:57.050
Come on, let's make it a reality.

00:50:01.050 --> 00:50:04.570
Here we are, in the dark and creepy
crooked forest.

00:50:04.571 --> 00:50:06.610
In search of the mythical unicorn.

00:50:07.050 --> 00:50:08.050
For some reason.

00:50:08.470 --> 00:50:11.310
And here she is, the fearless unicorn
hunter.

00:50:11.690 --> 00:50:13.070
It can eat us, stop it!

00:50:13.350 --> 00:50:15.230
You're gonna scare away the unicorn.

00:50:15.590 --> 00:50:19.370
If somehow we actually find a unicorn,
I'm gonna film it and get rich.

00:50:19.870 --> 00:50:20.970
Look over there!

00:50:24.360 --> 00:50:26.580
This is it, this is where we're gonna see
it.

00:50:28.060 --> 00:50:29.740
Unicorns, here we come!

00:50:30.640 --> 00:50:31.640
What's that for?

00:50:31.880 --> 00:50:32.440
Bait!

00:50:32.700 --> 00:50:33.700
Duh.

00:50:33.780 --> 00:50:34.780
Come on!

00:50:37.180 --> 00:50:39.300
Now all we have to do is wait.

00:50:43.860 --> 00:50:45.160
Okay, this is Brad's lair.

00:50:45.400 --> 00:50:47.421
It may not look like much,
but this place is armed

00:50:47.422 --> 00:50:50.100
with some of the most high-tech
weaponry known to man.

00:50:50.660 --> 00:50:52.440
It's considered impenetrable.

00:50:52.920 --> 00:50:55.120
But a piece of cake for us, right,
brother?

00:50:56.100 --> 00:50:59.520
Yes, this is not like stealing lollipops.

00:51:01.700 --> 00:51:02.700
Whoa!

00:51:04.530 --> 00:51:08.890
This security system can detect an air
assault from any direction.

00:51:12.710 --> 00:51:16.230
So we'll have to approach low and close to
the water.

00:51:17.170 --> 00:51:18.170
Next.

00:51:19.570 --> 00:51:21.810
Then there are these deadly spikes.

00:51:24.910 --> 00:51:28.170
Covered with enough poison to blow your
mind.

00:51:28.970 --> 00:51:29.970
Literally.

00:51:31.690 --> 00:51:33.030
Good to know.

00:51:33.270 --> 00:51:34.170
So here's the plan.

00:51:34.171 --> 00:51:36.850
You're the getaway driver.

00:51:37.410 --> 00:51:38.970
So you'll wait in the boat.

00:51:39.090 --> 00:51:40.010
Wait, hold on.

00:51:40.050 --> 00:51:41.170
Wait in the boat?

00:51:41.370 --> 00:51:43.950
But I want to be in on the actions.

00:51:45.670 --> 00:51:49.250
Through the getaway driver is the most
crucial part of any plan.

00:51:49.570 --> 00:51:51.870
Do you know how hard it is?

00:51:52.210 --> 00:51:54.950
Doing nothing, touching
nothing, with all of

00:51:54.951 --> 00:51:57.030
the adrenaline coursing
through your veins.

00:51:57.270 --> 00:51:58.270
And you must wait.

00:51:58.890 --> 00:52:00.190
Can I count on you?

00:52:01.090 --> 00:52:01.410
No.

00:52:02.110 --> 00:52:03.450
I guess so.

00:52:03.451 --> 00:52:06.670
So I'll climb up to the cube and enter
here.

00:52:07.430 --> 00:52:09.790
And once I'm inside, find the diamond.

00:52:10.330 --> 00:52:12.210
I've underestimated Brad before.

00:52:12.710 --> 00:52:13.990
It's not going to be easy.

00:52:14.470 --> 00:52:16.710
I think we can handle it.

00:52:19.190 --> 00:52:20.410
That's villain suits!

00:52:20.650 --> 00:52:22.070
This will make us unstoppable!

00:52:23.330 --> 00:52:23.670
Whoa!

00:52:23.730 --> 00:52:24.930
Achoo-wah-wah!

00:52:25.250 --> 00:52:26.330
I call the black one!

00:52:29.650 --> 00:52:31.350
It's call time!

00:52:41.850 --> 00:52:42.850
Hello.

00:52:43.570 --> 00:52:44.570
Oh, hi.

00:52:44.730 --> 00:52:46.230
Hello, Mother Margo.

00:52:46.630 --> 00:52:47.630
I am Nico.

00:52:47.950 --> 00:52:51.830
I present you a pig to confirm my
engagement to your daughter.

00:52:53.590 --> 00:52:55.750
Hey, what now?

00:52:55.890 --> 00:52:56.890
What's going on?

00:52:56.930 --> 00:52:57.930
Remember Little Boots?

00:52:58.470 --> 00:53:00.470
Hello, my schmoopsy-poo.

00:53:00.550 --> 00:53:01.550
Whoa, hey.

00:53:01.730 --> 00:53:03.130
You seem to think you're engaged.

00:53:04.530 --> 00:53:05.110
What?

00:53:05.350 --> 00:53:06.370
We're not engaged.

00:53:06.870 --> 00:53:09.770
Look, Nico, you seem like a very nice boy.

00:53:09.771 --> 00:53:11.310
With a very nice pig.

00:53:11.650 --> 00:53:13.270
But you're not engaged.

00:53:14.530 --> 00:53:14.930
Okay?

00:53:15.130 --> 00:53:16.250
It's not happening.

00:53:17.190 --> 00:53:18.250
I understand.

00:53:19.130 --> 00:53:20.130
Who was I kidding?

00:53:20.410 --> 00:53:23.590
A dumpling like me with a goddess like
you.

00:53:24.270 --> 00:53:27.630
But I promise, I will never forget you,
Margo.

00:53:28.630 --> 00:53:29.630
Never.

00:53:31.070 --> 00:53:33.690
Oh, I'm pretty sure I won't forget you
either.

00:53:34.110 --> 00:53:34.630
Bye.

00:53:34.770 --> 00:53:35.770
Bye, Nico.

00:53:36.450 --> 00:53:37.650
Wow, that was crazy.

00:53:37.651 --> 00:53:41.050
Whoa, that was totally humiliating.

00:53:41.330 --> 00:53:44.010
Taking a bite of that cheese was the
stupidest thing I've ever done.

00:53:44.410 --> 00:53:45.570
Why did I listen to you?

00:53:45.870 --> 00:53:47.770
Right, but it's over now, so...

00:53:48.890 --> 00:53:49.550
Here we go.

00:53:49.870 --> 00:53:50.870
Nico.

00:53:52.310 --> 00:53:55.170
You refuse my son's engagement,
pig?

00:53:55.370 --> 00:53:55.790
What?

00:53:56.030 --> 00:53:59.362
May you and your daughter
die a slow death and.

00:54:03.122 --> 00:54:03.390
..

00:54:03.391 --> 00:54:04.890
All right, lady, that's it.

00:54:05.250 --> 00:54:08.870
Nobody, nobody curses my daughter.

00:54:09.150 --> 00:54:10.170
You got that?

00:54:10.171 --> 00:54:13.510
Because if you mess with Margo,
you mess with me.

00:54:13.630 --> 00:54:17.790
And I promise you do not want to mess with
me.

00:54:18.090 --> 00:54:20.150
Do you understand me?

00:54:20.370 --> 00:54:21.370
Yes, yes.

00:54:21.570 --> 00:54:21.830
Good.

00:54:22.530 --> 00:54:23.530
Now, get!

00:54:27.650 --> 00:54:30.430
Look, Margo, I think we just need to...

00:54:35.500 --> 00:54:36.880
I have to tell Gru.

00:54:53.520 --> 00:54:55.040
Can we go back now?

00:54:55.340 --> 00:54:55.900
Already?

00:54:55.901 --> 00:54:57.980
Just a couple more hours.

00:54:58.240 --> 00:55:00.160
We have to be home before it gets dark.

00:55:00.520 --> 00:55:02.780
I don't understand.

00:55:03.600 --> 00:55:05.620
I did exactly what the man said.

00:55:05.900 --> 00:55:08.980
You mean that one-eyed, scar-faced man
that everybody laughed at?

00:55:09.240 --> 00:55:11.200
Yeah, it makes no sense.

00:55:11.600 --> 00:55:14.680
Look, Agnes, maybe we're not...

00:55:24.880 --> 00:55:28.160
My whole life has been building through
this moment!

00:55:35.370 --> 00:55:37.231
It's a... Unicorn!

00:55:39.290 --> 00:55:41.270
I can't believe it!

00:55:41.810 --> 00:55:43.870
I'm gonna name you Lucky!

00:55:44.990 --> 00:55:47.130
Oh, Lucky, stop it!

00:55:48.790 --> 00:55:51.310
Yeah, I'll let someone else burst her
bubble.

00:55:58.540 --> 00:56:02.080
Look at us, two brothers pulling the
heist!

00:56:02.440 --> 00:56:07.780
And that diamond will make us the richest,
most powerful villains in the world!

00:56:08.140 --> 00:56:09.140
Right, brother?

00:56:15.760 --> 00:56:16.760
Bravo!

00:56:17.320 --> 00:56:18.320
Bravo, Simo!

00:56:18.680 --> 00:56:19.300
You're amazing!

00:56:19.560 --> 00:56:21.795
I'm so sorry I'm so
embarrassed, I was very

00:56:21.796 --> 00:56:23.720
rude, and you were
always such a gentleman!

00:56:23.740 --> 00:56:24.140
You did it!

00:56:24.160 --> 00:56:25.580
You got our jobs back!

00:56:32.280 --> 00:56:34.220
Oh yeah, right, sure!

00:56:34.860 --> 00:56:35.860
Oh look, we're here!

00:56:43.340 --> 00:56:44.360
I'm going in!

00:56:44.440 --> 00:56:45.440
Take the wheel!

00:56:45.500 --> 00:56:48.100
I still don't see why I can't go with you!

00:56:48.101 --> 00:56:52.360
Hey, hey, we discussed this, now is not
the time to mess with the plant!

00:56:52.860 --> 00:56:53.860
Fine.

00:56:56.420 --> 00:56:57.420
I

00:57:09.540 --> 00:57:11.800
told you, you're supposed to stay with the
boat!

00:57:11.920 --> 00:57:14.880
Oh, I didn't think you meant that
literally.

00:57:15.080 --> 00:57:16.560
What other way could I have meant it?

00:57:17.780 --> 00:57:18.980
Alright, let's move.

00:57:19.220 --> 00:57:20.500
Just follow my lead.

00:57:21.400 --> 00:57:22.400
Got it!

00:57:26.180 --> 00:57:27.180
Help me!

00:57:27.280 --> 00:57:28.420
Ow, ow, ow!

00:57:28.620 --> 00:57:29.080
Oh no!

00:57:29.081 --> 00:57:30.200
Where's the bikes?

00:57:30.760 --> 00:57:32.570
They're gonna be bailed!

00:57:35.060 --> 00:57:36.520
I'm okay!

00:57:37.740 --> 00:57:39.120
I miss the minions.

00:57:39.700 --> 00:57:40.700
Come on!

00:57:46.200 --> 00:57:47.420
Coming!

00:57:54.000 --> 00:57:55.000
Coming!

00:58:07.080 --> 00:58:08.560
It's a scaling device!

00:58:09.040 --> 00:58:10.240
Quick, camouflage mold!

00:58:11.600 --> 00:58:11.860
Freeze!

00:58:12.420 --> 00:58:13.420
And close your eyes!

00:58:13.460 --> 00:58:14.460
And cover your mouth!

